A pot of milk is ruined by a drop of poison Don't put the cart before =
the horse




There are no small parts, only small actors Heaven protects children, =
sailors and drunken men Home is where the heart is
It's a good horse that never stumbles There's no arguing with the barrel =
of a gun Variety is the spice of life
Loose lips sink ships Purely bluster and no substance
A little knowledge is dangerous Drink deep, or taste not the puritan =
waters Great minds think alike, but insanity speaks all languages - John =
Parry If something can go wrong, it will (Murphy's Law)
It's often a person's mouth broke their nose No gain without pain Whom =
we love best, to them we can say the least Joined proverb: A stitch in =
time will save the cracked pitcher from going longest to the well
The highest attainable level of quality (also used is: Good as Greg) =
You'll always miss 100% of the [basketball] shots you don't take =
Possible Interpretation: What you do now reflects upon what will happen =
later
Possible Interpretation: All style and no substance There are no Facts; =
only interpretations of Facts
Interpretation: If you are going to do something, do it right Never do =
today what you can put off till (until) tomorrow  A chain is no stronger =
than its weakest link
Everyone wants to go to heaven but no-one wants to die Alternative: =
Treat 'im rough, you get you muff--Ali G We all make mistakes Half a =
loaf is better than none
Sex is like war, both are exciting but neither informative Variant for =
slow risers: The early worm gets eaten by the birds If you live each day =
as if it was your last, someday you'll most certainly be right
Trouble shared is trouble halved The more things change, the more they =
stay the same Going the whole nine yards He who dares wins (motto of the =
Special Air Service (aka SAS))
If it isn't broke, don't fix it Well begun is half done Alternative: Who =
guards the guardians? Possible Interpretation: You can't get away with a =
lie, it will always reveal the truth someday Grow where you are planted
A good beginning makes a good ending It is not so much the gift that is =
given but the way in which the gift is driven Looking at a horse's mouth =
is one classic way to judge it's health
